  "title": "Rights & Liberties",
  "description": "The modern charter of the citizen — human rights, equality, information rights and data protection.",
  "custodian": "Ministry of Justice · Government Equalities Office",
  "polity": "uk",
  "preamble": "# Rights & Liberties\n\nIf the Constitutional Instruments codex records what the state may not do to Parliament,\nthis codex records what the state may not do to *you*. Its four statutes form the\nmodern charter of the citizen: the rights you hold against public authorities, the\nequality you are owed by employers and services, your right to know what the state\nknows, and your rights over data about yourself.\n\n## Documents in this codex\n\n| Document | Citation | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Human Rights Act 1998 | 1998 c. 42 | In force |\n| Freedom of Information Act 2000 | 2000 c. 36 | In force |\n| Equality Act 2010 | 2010 c. 15 | In force (amended) |\n| Data Protection Act 2018 | 2018 c. 12 | In force (amended) |\n\n## Why these live together\n\nEach of these Acts gives the individual an enforceable claim against power — in court\n(Human Rights Act), in the workplace and marketplace (Equality Act), and against the\nstate's information asymmetry (Freedom of Information, Data Protection). They share\nenforcement institutions (the courts, the Information Commissioner, the Equality and\nHuman Rights Commission) and are routinely litigated together.",
